<% content_for :title, "Select" %>
<%
  timezones = [
    ["Auckland", "auckland"], ["Berlin", "berlin"], ["Bogotá", "bogota"], ["Cairo", "cairo"],
    ["Chicago", "chicago"], ["Delhi", "delhi"], ["Dublin", "dublin"], ["Helsinki", "helsinki"],
    ["Lagos", "lagos"], ["Lisbon", "lisbon"], ["London", "london"], ["Madrid", "madrid"],
    ["Nairobi", "nairobi"], ["New York", "new_york"], ["Oslo", "oslo"], ["Paris", "paris"],
    ["São Paulo", "sao_paulo"], ["Singapore", "singapore"], ["Sydney", "sydney"], ["Tokyo", "tokyo"]
  ]
  regions = {
    "Europe" => [["France", "fr"], ["Germany", "de"], ["Spain", "es"]],
    "Americas" => [["Brazil", "br"], ["Canada", "ca"], ["Mexico", "mx"]],
    "Asia" => [["India", "in"], ["Japan", "jp"], ["Singapore", "sg"]]
  }
  plans = [["Starter", "starter"], ["Growth", "growth"], ["Enterprise", "enterprise"]]
%>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Forms</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Select</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    One choice from a list Rails already has: a model's enum (<code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">model: Order, enum: :status</code>, labelled through
    <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">human_attribute_name</code>), a <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">belongs_to</code> collection read the way <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">collection_select</code> reads
    it, or an options array or hash. Inside a model-bound <%= link_to "Field", field_path, class: "text-primary underline" %> the
    record's value is selected and its errors shown. It renders a real <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;select&gt;</code>, mirrored into a WAI-ARIA
    combobox; the select is the only place the value lives, so it submits, validates <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">required</code>, resets with its
    form and still works with JavaScript off.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="select-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-start gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[timezone]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Timezone" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: timezones, selected: "london",
                            native_on_touch: false) %>
      <% field.with_description { "Used for every date we show you." } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[status]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Order status" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, model: DemoOrder, enum: :status, selected: "packed",
                            native_on_touch: false) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[country]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Country" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: regions, prompt: true, native_on_touch: false) %>
      <% field.with_description { "Grouped, the way grouped_collection_select renders." } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[plan]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Plan" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: plans, selected: "growth",
                            disabled_values: ["enterprise"], native_on_touch: false) %>
      <% field.with_description { "Enterprise is disabled: reachable, never selectable." } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[locked]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Region (locked)" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: plans, selected: "starter", disabled: true,
                            native_on_touch: false) %>
      <% field.with_description { "Disabled: out of the tab order, and it never submits." } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[plan_sm]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Plan (size: :sm)" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: plans, selected: "growth", size: :sm,
                            native_on_touch: false) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[plan_lg]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Plan (size: :lg)" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: plans, selected: "growth", size: :lg,
                            native_on_touch: false) %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Search %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">With search</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">search: true</code> switches the
  combobox to its editable mode: the WAI-ARIA combobox with list autocomplete. Typing filters the list, ignoring case and
  accents; nothing else in the API changes, and the value still lives in the same native select.
</p>
<div id="select-search-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-start gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[city]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "City" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: timezones, selected: "london", search: true,
                            include_blank: "No preference") %>
      <% field.with_description { "Type to filter. Empty the field to clear your choice." } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[favourite]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Favourite city" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: timezones, selected: "paris", search: true) %>
      <% field.with_description { "No blank option: there is always a value." } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="w-64">
    <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "demo[region]") do |field| %>
      <% field.with_label { "Region" } %>
      <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: regions, search: true, prompt: "Search regions") %>
      <% field.with_description { "Grouped: a group with nothing left in it is hidden." } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Inside a form %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">In a form</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  The select submits, blocks submission while <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">required</code>
  and blank, and resets with its form — none of which this component implements, because none of it is its to implement.
</p>
<div id="select-form-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-12 mb-8">
  <form id="select-form" action="<%= demo_submit_path %>" method="post" class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-4">
    <div class="w-64">
      <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "booking[timezone]") do |field| %>
        <% field.with_label { "Meeting timezone" } %>
        <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: timezones, selected: "berlin",
                              native_on_touch: false) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="w-64">
      <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "booking[plan]") do |field| %>
        <% field.with_label { "Plan (required)" } %>
        <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: plans, required: true, prompt: "Choose a plan",
                              native_on_touch: false) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="w-64">
      <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "booking[city]") do |field| %>
        <% field.with_label { "City (search)" } %>
        <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: timezones, search: true, include_blank: true) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="w-64">
      <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "booking[tier]") do |field| %>
        <% field.with_label { "Tier (locked)" } %>
        <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: plans, selected: "growth", disabled: true,
                              native_on_touch: false) %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(type: "submit")) { "Submit" } %>
    <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(type: "reset", variant: :outline)) { "Reset" } %>
  </form>
</div>

<%# Server round trip %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">A server round trip</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  A real form in a Turbo Frame. Submit it empty and the server answers 422 with the error on the Field; choose a city and
  the value comes back selected. Nothing here is Select's doing — the value is in a native
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;select&gt;</code>, so the
  round trip is the one Rails always had.
</p>
<div id="select-round-trip-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-12 mb-8">
  <%= render 'docs/select_round_trip', trip: DemoTrip.new, cities: DocsController.cities, submission: 0 %>
</div>

<%# In a Modal %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Inside a Modal</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  The popup is in the top layer, so it draws above the dialog and is not clipped by its scroll box. The first Escape
  closes the listbox and the second closes the Modal — that ordering is the browser's, not ours.
</p>
<div id="select-modal-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex items-center justify-center p-12 mb-8">
  <button type="button" id="select-modal-trigger"
          onclick="document.body.append(document.getElementById('select-modal-open').content.cloneNode(true))"
          class="rounded-md border border-border bg-background px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium hover:bg-muted transition-colors">
    Open a Modal with a Select
  </button>
</div>
<div id="select-modal"></div>
<template id="select-modal-open">
  <turbo-stream action="append" target="select-modal"><template>
    <%= render Ui::ModalComponent.new(aria: { labelledby: "select-modal-title" }) do %>
      <div class="p-6">
        <h2 id="select-modal-title" class="text-base font-semibold">Pick a city</h2>
        <p class="mt-1.5 mb-6 text-sm text-muted-foreground">A Select inside a dialog behaves exactly as it does outside one.</p>
        <div class="w-64">
          <%= render Ui::FieldComponent.new(name: "modal[city]") do |field| %>
            <% field.with_label { "City" } %>
            <% field.with_control(Ui::SelectComponent, options: timezones, selected: "london",
                                  native_on_touch: false) %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </template></turbo-stream>
</template>

<%# Standalone %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Without a Field</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  Outside a Field, name it yourself with <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria: { label: }</code>
  — it reaches both the select and the combobox.
</p>
<div id="select-standalone-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background p-12 mb-8">
  <div class="w-64">
    <%# native_on_touch is left at its default here, so this is the instance that shows the
        phone behaviour: on a coarse pointer it stays the native select and its platform picker %>
    <%= render Ui::SelectComponent.new(name: "standalone[plan]", options: plans, selected: "starter",
                                       aria: { label: "Billing plan" }) %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#select-usage" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="select-usage" class="text-card-foreground"><%= h(example_select_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Testing %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Testing host applications</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  Enhanced, the native select is laid under the combobox at
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">opacity: 0</code>, so Capybara's
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">select "Pending", from: "Status"</code>
  no longer picks what a person would. The kit ships a helper that drives the widget instead —
  include it once and your existing tests read the same. It fails with the Select's name and the options it does offer,
  and raises on an ambiguous name rather than writing to the wrong control.
</p>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-muted px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Ruby</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#select-helper-usage" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-card px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="select-helper-usage" class="text-card-foreground"><%= h(example_ui_select_helper) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["name",               "String",        "required", "The control's HTML name, e.g. \"post[author_id]\". The id is derived from it the way form_with derives one."],
        ["collection",         "Enumerable",    "nil",      "With value_method: and text_method:, exactly as collection_select takes them. Each accepts a symbol or a proc."],
        ["options",            "Array or Hash", "nil",      "What options_for_select takes: [\"S\", \"M\"], [[\"Draft\", \"draft\"]], { \"Draft\" => \"draft\" }, or { \"Europe\" => [[\"France\", \"fr\"]] } for groups."],
        ["model / enum",       "Class, Symbol", "nil",      "A model and one of its enums. Labels come from human_attribute_name; the submitted value is the enum key."],
        ["group_method",       "Symbol/Proc",   "nil",      "With group_label_method:, the grouped_collection_select shape."],
        ["selected",           "Object",        "nil",      "Compared by string value, as Rails' helpers compare it."],
        ["include_blank",      "Boolean/String","false",    "Rails' include_blank: true renders an empty option, a string labels it."],
        ["prompt",             "Boolean/String","nil",      "Renders only while nothing is selected. true uses Rails' own helpers.select.prompt."],
        ["disabled_values",    "Array",         "nil",      "Options that are reachable by keyboard but never selectable."],
        ["required",           "Boolean",       "false",    "Sets required on the select, and adds the empty option Rails adds when there is no blank or prompt."],
        ["disabled",           "Boolean",       "false",    "Disables the select, so it never submits, and takes the combobox out of the tab order."],
        ["search",             "Boolean",       "false",    "Switches the combobox to its editable, filtering mode."],
        ["size",               "Symbol",        ":default", "One of :sm, :default, :lg — the heights Button's sizes have. The combobox, the select under it and search mode's show-options button all take it; the popup keeps matching the control's width."],
        ["native_on_touch",    "Boolean",       "true",     "On a coarse pointer, select-only mode stays the native select and its platform picker. Search mode always enhances."],
        ["class",              "String",        "nil",      "Merged over the control's default classes -- the caller always wins."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Keyboard %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Keyboard</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  The WAI-ARIA select-only combobox pattern, key for key. DOM focus never leaves the combobox: the active option is
  announced through <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-activedescendant</code>.
</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">State</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Key</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Result</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["closed", "↓, Alt+↓, Enter, Space", "Opens without moving visual focus or changing the selection; the active option is the selected one."],
        ["closed", "↑", "Opens, then moves visual focus to the first option."],
        ["closed", "Home / End", "Opens and moves visual focus to the first / last option."],
        ["closed or open", "printable characters", "Opens if closed, then typeahead: first match, full-string match in quick succession, cycling on a repeated character."],
        ["open", "↓ / ↑", "Next / previous option. At either end, visual focus stays put."],
        ["open", "Home / End", "First / last option."],
        ["open", "PageUp / PageDown", "Up / down ten options, or to the first / last."],
        ["open", "Enter, Space, Alt+↑", "Selects the active option, closes, visual focus back on the combobox."],
        ["open", "Tab", "Selects the active option, closes, and focus moves on."],
        ["open", "Escape", "Closes with no change."],
      ].each do |state, key, result| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= state %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= key %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= result %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-3">Search mode</h3>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-3">
  The editable combobox with list autocomplete. The text field never submits — it has no
  <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">name</code> — and what you type is
  never turned into a value: only a real option can be chosen.
</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">State</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Key</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Result</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["closed", "↓ / ↑", "Opens and moves visual focus to the first / last option."],
        ["closed", "Alt+↓", "Opens without moving visual focus."],
        ["closed", "Escape", "Puts the text back to the selected option's label. It never changes the value: clearing a choice is what a blank option is for."],
        ["closed", "Enter", "Not handled: the form submits, exactly as it would from any text field."],
        ["closed or open", "typing", "Opens if closed, and filters the list — ignoring case and accents."],
        ["open", "↓ / ↑", "Next / previous option, wrapping."],
        ["open", "Enter", "Takes the active option if there is one, and closes either way. Never submits while the list is open."],
        ["open", "Escape", "Closes; the text goes back to the selected option's label."],
        ["open", "←, →, Home, End, typing", "Visual focus returns to the text field and the key edits the text."],
        ["open", "Tab", "Closes without selecting: what you typed is never turned into a choice."],
      ].each do |state, key, result| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= state %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= key %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= result %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Behaviour %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Behaviour</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>The native <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">&lt;select&gt;</code> is the only value store. To change the value from your own code, set <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">select.value</code> and dispatch <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">change</code> — there is no second API.</li>
  <li>Choosing an option dispatches <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">input</code> and <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">change</code> from the select, so <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">ui--form-change</code>, an auto-submitting form and your own <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">change-&gt;</code> action all keep working. Choosing what is already chosen dispatches nothing.</li>
  <li>Options change by re-rendering the component — a Turbo Stream <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">replace</code> of its root or of the Field around it. A stream that patches individual options is unsupported: it would desync the select from the listbox.</li>
  <li>On a phone, select-only mode stays the native select, so you get the platform picker. Pass <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">native_on_touch: false</code> to enhance everywhere.</li>
  <li>In search mode a click on the text field places the caret; the chevron button beside it opens the list, which is also what a touch screen-reader user reaches for. Typing opens it too.</li>
  <li>Escape is the cancel key in both modes: with the list open it closes it, and on a closed search field it puts the text back to the selected option's label. It never changes the value, so a dependent select or an auto-save never sees a change the user meant as "never mind". This is a deliberate deviation from the APG key table, where the text field <em>is</em> the value.</li>
  <li>Search filters the listbox, never the select: the option that would post is never hidden away. A group with nothing left in it is hidden, and an empty result shows <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">rails_ui_kit.select.no_results</code> while the count is announced in a polite live region once typing settles.</li>
</ul>

<%# Accessibility %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>The combobox is named by the Field's label, and described by its description and error; <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-invalid</code> and
      <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">required</code> are on the element a screen reader is on.</li>
  <li>Focus never leaves the combobox. The active option is announced through <code class="text-xs bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-activedescendant</code>, and in
      search mode the number of results is announced once typing settles.</li>
  <li>Where it isn't enhanced — JavaScript off, or select-only mode on a phone — the user has the platform's own select,
      which is fully accessible on its own.</li>
</ul>

<%# Not this %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  A handful of options the user should compare at a glance are radios: <%= link_to "Choices", choices_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>.
  So is picking several from a short list, as checkboxes; a searchable multi-select isn't built yet. A value that isn't from a
  known list is an <%= link_to "Input", input_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>. An action menu is a
  <%= link_to "Dropdown", dropdown_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>, not a select.
</p>
